      en: "El Factor is a municipality in the María Trinidad Sánchez province of the Dominican Republic, located approximately 10 kilometers south of the Samaná Bay coast. The local economy is predominantly agricultural, focusing on rice, cacao, and coffee cultivation. It was officially designated as a municipality on November 18, 1992. The tropical climate averages 25 °C year-round. El Factor offers a glimpse into rural Dominican life, with its quiet streets and community-oriented markets. The area's history is tied to the expansion of farming settlements in the northeastern region.",
